    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d43">

                <pb facs="0090" n="83" sameAs="frus:frus1894Nicaragua/pg83"/>

                <head>No. 43.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Guzman to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the Republic of Nicaragua</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1894-05-10"><hi rendition="#italic">May 10,
                                1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Pursuant to the conversation I had with
                    your excellency on the 7th instant, I have sent to the President of Nicaragua a
                    cable gram in which I state that the Government of the United States would be
                        <pb facs="0091" n="84" xml:id="pg84"/> pleased to see that the-utmost
                    harmony may prevail between Nicaragua and the canal company, and that it would
                    be much gratified if all proceedings against the said company were revoked.</p>
                <p>I reiterate, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. Guzman.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
